{
  "dom_id": "step-q129192",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x-y+z-1}$ that passes through the point $P(1,1,1).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1,1) & ={e}^{1-1+1-1} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {e}^{x-y+z-1} & =1 \\\\ x-y+z-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(1,1,1)$ is the plane $x-y+z-1=0.$",
